From 1839762a6e224cc91a37aa5d5f6a8a00ae7f2edc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: indextree <hellonypcteam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:06:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Replace the unsound circom verifier with generated
 circuit-specific verifiers

Upstream VerifyGKR(meta): initial claim hard-coded to 0 and D unused;
sumcheck challenges, r*, and all points z were free prover inputs; no final
layer check against add~/mult~ wiring; round-polynomial length = max over
proofs (no degree bound); input evaluation via unconstrained '<--'
(evalMultivariate/evalGateFunction). An all-zero 'proof' verified for any
circuit.

Now circom_codegen::gkr_verifier_template emits a template per GKR circuit
with the wiring, fixed inputs, digest and claimed output as constants; it
recomputes every challenge with the circomlib MultiMiMC7 transcript
(identical to rust/python), enforces 3 coefficients per round and k+1 for q,
checks each layer against add~/mult~ via constrained eq tables, and checks the
constrained input MLE. The aggregator passes (circuit, input, proof)
artifacts between rounds and uses the generated templates.
